        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00080",
          "explanation": "Doctor gives a directly usable opening sentence for the consultation, including diabetes and medication, that the family can recite verbatim.",
          "quote": "他左桡神经损害，肌电图提示损伤严重、保守治疗效果不好，现在左手麻、手背无力、拿东西不稳，还有肌肉变瘦，并且有糖尿病，麻烦评估是不是需要周围神经/神经修复方向进一步处理"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The doctor converted the family's real-world constraints (fear of missing information, not knowing what to say) into an executable checklist and communication script. The family was given a concrete packet list and a pre-written opening sentence that integrates privacy-sensitive diabetes disclosure. This is clearly beyond the basic RC6 requirement of forming a plan.",
      "ho_id": "HO3",
      "meaningful_trajectory_impact": true,
      "triggered": true
    },
    {
      "active_model_action": true,
      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00031",
          "explanation": "Doctor corrects the family's implicit assumption that 'no obvious contraindication' means zero risk and that surgery will definitely make things worse.",
          "quote": "手术会不会越做越坏？任何手术都有风险，但对于明确的、严重的神经卡压，手术的根本目的是解除压迫、为神经再生创造条件"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "The family initially expressed fear that surgery might make the hand worse and that not operating would lead to permanent loss. The doctor explicitly acknowledged the worry, corrected the misconception that surgery is a high-risk gamble, and reframed it as a necessary intervention to prevent permanent atrophy. The family then accepted the corrected plan and proceeded with the appointment. This repaired a specific, documented misconception in the trajectory.",
      "ho_id": "HO4",
